{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ypb24alwaqbmzc4ubc6dehfnjxp3vywbksfybxodi7ltcdofcbuq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. Everything passes from a clean slate.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Configuration surface:** `Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]` section** and `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` has no `option()`/`target_compile_definitions`/`#ifdef` — so there is exactly **one** valid build configuration. `run_all_features.sh` still enumerates it mechanically (power-set of `[features]`) and, for extra coverage, re-runs the whole suite against the **optimised release `.so`** as well as the debug one.\n\n**Phase A artifacts** (crate root):\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — 4/4 C symbols (`gotomach`, `process_value`, `double_value`, `triple_value`) exported by the Rust `.so`; 0 missing, 0 non-libc undefined. The four `static` C helpers are correctly *not* exported by either.\n- `ERRORS.md` — 17 rejection rows mechanically derived from every `return`/`goto cleanup`/guard in `lib.c`, plus G1–G7 generic FFI boundary cases.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 51 rows over the real branch axes (`mode` 0/1/2/`default:`, `iterations` shapes incl. 0/1/65534/65535, `seed` shapes, 6 `threshold` regimes incl. exact strict-`<` boundary, `count` saturation, and the three low-level `operation_fn` entry points called directly and composed).\n\n**Tests** (`tests/`, all via `libloading` on both `.so`s — never calling Rust directly): 71 tests, 51 Phase B + 14 Phase C + 6 Phase D. Each compares the `int` return per input **and** the complete captured stdout byte stream (the `printf`/`puts` log lines), using a fixed-seed xorshift PRNG (~68 000 `gotomach` calls and ~110 000 op calls per implementation per run).\n\n**No Rust fixes were needed** — the translation was already byte-identical. So I hardened against false confidence instead:\n\n- **Mutation testing** (14 injected bugs, each built + run + reverted): every one was caught — wrong arithmetic, `<`→`<=` acceptance, `%1001` feedback, off-by-one bounds, wrong error sentinels, guard reordering, `malloc(0)` misinterpreted as failure, deleted log lines, and a deleted `free`. The single survivor (`is_valid_state` `<`→`<=`) is a **provably equivalent mutant** — `count ≤ i < iterations == capacity`, so that branch is unreachable through the public API, which is exactly what `ERRORS.md` rows 8/17 document.\n- **Anti-vacuity guards:** `d0` asserts the two libraries are distinct files whose symbols resolve to *different* addresses; the batch driver fails if stdout capture yields 0 bytes; `symbol_parity.sh` fails if either symbol list is empty.\n\nTwo real bugs found — **in my own harness**, not the translation: `symbol_parity.sh` was writing temp files to a read-only `/tmp` and reporting a vacuous PASS (fixed to use `mktemp` under `$TMPDIR` + empty-list guards, validated with a negative control against `libz.so.1` → exit 1); and one mutation initially \"survived\" only because `cargo build` had failed and the stale `.so` was reused (the mutation runner now verifies the build).\n\n`c_src/` was not modified (only the `build/` output directory was created, per the task instructions)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":781,"cache_read_input_tokens":130705,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":781,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6136b9ea-c933-4b26-9cc6-f91d0068bdc5","uuid":"da4a0f9d-b476-449a-80b4-ae18782978d8","timestamp":"2026-08-19T20:37:36.364Z"}
